# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  .dockerignore — Prevents bloat and secret leaks in Docker images
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  WHY THIS MATTERS:
#  When Docker builds an image, it sends the ENTIRE build context (your
#  project directory) to the Docker daemon. Without .dockerignore, this
#  includes:
#    - .git/ (can be 100s of MB)
#    - Model checkpoints (GB)
#    - Training data (GB)
#    - .env files (secrets!)
#    - __pycache__/ and .pyc files
#    - Virtual environments (thousands of files)
#
#  This slows down builds, bloats image layers, and can leak secrets
#  into the image filesystem (discoverable via 'docker history').
#

# ─── Version Control ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ─── Secrets (NEVER include in image) ────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Model Checkpoints & Data ───────────────────────────────────────────
checkpoints/
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/tokenized/
data/split/
data/sft/
data/preference/
tokenizers/
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors

# ─── Python Artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# ─── Test & Coverage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ─── IDE & Editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ─── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log

# ─── Docker ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml

# ─── Documentation (not needed in runtime image) ────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
LICENSE

# ─── Misc ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.run/
wandb/
mlruns/
